# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC <a id="section-2"></a>
# MAGIC ## 2. Horizontal scaling: more than one instance behind one URL
# MAGIC **The idea:** run the app on **1-5 instances** behind the same URL. You get higher availability, more concurrency, **zero-downtime deployments** and best-effort **session affinity** (sticky sessions). Compute cost scales linearly with the instance count, so add instances when traffic needs them. Horizontal scaling is GA (September 2026).
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **How (new app):** **Databricks Apps > + Create app > Create a custom app**, then in the **Configure** step select **Enable horizontal scaling** and set the **Number of instances**. Databricks recommends at least 2 for availability.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **Before you switch:**
# MAGIC * New horizontally scaled apps **don't include the pre-installed Python libraries**, so declare every dependency in `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml`.
# MAGIC * Per-user in-memory state is only best-effort sticky. Anything that MUST survive a restart or an instance change belongs in a database, which is what section 3 covers.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Docs: *Horizontal scaling for Databricks apps*.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC [↑ Back to contents](#contents)

# COMMAND ----------

# DBTITLE 1,Read-only: list apps in this workspace and their current compute settings
# Read-only: list apps in this workspace and their current compute settings.
from databricks.sdk import WorkspaceClient
w = WorkspaceClient()
for a in w.apps.list():
    print(a.name, "|", getattr(a, "compute_size", None), "|", a.url)

# COMMAND ----------

