# MAGIC <a id="section-3"></a>
# MAGIC ## 3. Lakebase app templates: give the app its own state
# MAGIC **The idea:** if the app needs to store its own data (user inputs, workflow status, edits), back it with **Lakebase**, the managed Postgres database in Databricks, instead of files or in-memory state. Lakebase scales compute automatically.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **Fastest start:** **Databricks Apps > + Create app**, open the **Database** tab and pick one of the Lakebase templates (**Dash, Flask or Streamlit**, built around a to-do app). It deploys with example code showing the connection pattern end to end.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **For an existing app:** add a Lakebase resource to the app (`app.resources.postgres` for new apps). Docs: *Using Lakebase with Databricks Apps* and *Add a Lakebase resource to a Databricks app*.
